course: dictionary
lesson: 411
title: One word, many meanings: apply
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one is meant. The word apply is a good example. You can apply cream to your skin, apply for a school place, or apply a rule to a new problem. The context tells you which meaning to use.
explain: «Consistency means applying rules the same way to everyone; treating two people differently for the same thing seems unfair unless there is a real difference.» Here applying means using a rule. The clue words are rules and everyone: the same rule is used the same way for each person.
explain: «An exception is a case where a rule does not apply; families and groups can agree on exceptions together.» Does apply mean put on a surface here? No. It means the rule does not reach that case. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: Apply is a verb: apply, applies, applied, applying.
fact: To apply something means to put it on a surface, like cream on skin or glue on paper.
fact: To apply for something means to ask for it officially, often by filling in a form, like a job or a school place.
fact: To apply a rule or idea means to use it in a situation, and a rule applies to someone when it is about them.
fact: «Exception» means a case where a rule does not apply.
exercise: «Mum asked me to apply sun cream before we went to the beach.» What does apply mean here? | To ask for a job at the beach | To wash the cream off | To use a rule about the sea | *To put cream on my skin
exercise: «Consistency means applying rules the same way to everyone.» What is being applied in this sentence? | A plaster | Cream | *Rules | A form for a school place
exercise: Which meaning of apply is ask for something officially, often on a form? | Apply sun cream to your arms | Apply glue to paper | *Apply for a school place | Apply a rule to a new game
test: «An exception is a case where a rule does not apply.» What does the rule does not apply mean? | *The rule is not used in that case | The rule is pressed very hard | The rule is asked for on a form | The rule is painted on a wall
test: Jayden says apply always means cream. What is the best reply? | *No, apply can also mean to ask for something officially, like a job | Yes, it always means cream | Yes, but only on paper | No, it only means a rule
exam: Which phrase uses apply to mean ask for something officially? | Apply glue to the card | Apply the rule to the game | Apply sun cream | *Apply for a school place
